name: sim.interpolateMatrices
description: Computes the interpolated transformation matrix between matrixIn1 and matrixIn2. Quaternions are used internally
luaSynopsis: list resultMatrix = sim.interpolateMatrices(list matrixIn1, list matrixIn2, float interpolFactor)
pythonSynopsis: float[12] resultMatrix = sim.interpolateMatrices(float[12] matrixIn1, float[12] matrixIn2, float interpolFactor)
inputs:
1. matrixIn1: first input matrix (array of 12 values [Vx0 Vy0 Vz0 P0 Vx1 Vy1 Vz1 P1 Vx2 Vy2 Vz2 P2])
2. matrixIn2: second input matrix (array of 12 values [Vx0 Vy0 Vz0 P0 Vx1 Vy1 Vz1 P1 Vx2 Vy2 Vz2 P2])
3. interpolFactor: interpolation factor, a value between 0.0 and 1.0 (0.0--> resultMatrix = matrixIn1, 1.0--> resultMatrix = matrixIn2)
outputs:
1. resultMatrix: the result matrix (array of 12 values [Vx0 Vy0 Vz0 P0 Vx1 Vy1 Vz1 P1 Vx2 Vy2 Vz2 P2])
